{
 "text": " I didn't expect a $30 gift to cause this much chaos at our family Christmas. My brother-in-law steals them from my cousin. My cousin steals them back. My uncle freezes them. It became the gift nobody wanted to give up. Everyone else brought candles and gift cards. I brought five of these Luxe Light headlamps. The first time someone tried the motion sensor, the whole room went quiet. Just wave your hand. Light turns on. Wave again. Off. No fumbling with buttons. My nephew, who works construction, puts his on. Goes outside to his truck. Comes back 10 minutes later, still wearing it. Says it's better than the $50 headlamp his company bought him. The wide beam lights up everything at once. Not just one tiny spot like regular headlamps. You can see your whole work area without constantly turning your head. My mom uses hers for morning dog walks. Loves that when her hands are full with the leash, she can turn it on and off with a wave. Small enough to fit in a stocking, charges with USB-C, and people get genuinely excited when they try it. Oh, and they just dropped new limited edition colors too. Pink and orange. Which honestly make great gifts if you want to pick the color to match the person. Every single one comes with a free carry case as well. So they're basically gift ready out of the box. Right now, they've got up to 50% off. Which is how I managed to grab five of them. Best Christmas gift I've given that everyone actually fought over.",
